CHAPTER III
RIGHTS OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN
FROM ACTS OF VIOLENCE
Article 4
Women and children victims of acts of violence shall receive the following rights:
a. the right to have their dignity and worth as human beings respected;
b. the right to health and psychological recovery from the suffering experienced by the victim;
c. the right to determine their own decisions;
d. the right to obtain information;
e. the right to confidentiality;
f. the right to compensation;
g. the right to social rehabilitation;
h. the right to complaint handling;
i. the right of victims and their families to obtain facilitation in the judicial process; and
j. the right to assistance.

Article 5
Child victims of acts of violence, in addition to obtaining the rights as referred to in Article 4, also obtain special rights, as follows:
a. the right to respect and full utilization for survival, growth and development;
b. the right to basic services;
c. the right to equal protection;
d. the right to be free from various stigma; and
e. the right to obtain freedom;

Article 3
The objectives of protection of women and children from acts of violence, are to:
a. prevent acts of violence against women and children including trafficking in persons;
b. eliminate all forms of violence and exploitation against women and children;
c. protect, provide a sense of security for women and children;
d. provide services to women and children victims of acts of violence, reporters, and witnesses; and
e. facilitate and conduct mediation of domestic disputes to realize the integrity of a harmonious and prosperous household.

REGIONAL REGULATION OF THE SPECIAL CAPITAL REGION
PROVINCE OF JAKARTA
NUMBER 8 OF 2011
CONCERNING
PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN FROM ACTS OF VIOLENCE
BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD
THE GOVERNOR OF THE SPECIAL CAPITAL REGION PROVINCE OF JAKARTA,

Considering a. that discrimination and violence against women and children constitute violations of human rights, and crimes against humanity, and are inconsistent with the position of the Special Capital Region Province of Jakarta as the Capital of the Unitary State of the Republic of Indonesia;

b. that in the context of fulfilling the constitutional rights of women and children and to improve the quality of life of women and children is one of the mandatory affairs that is the duty, authority, and responsibility of the Regional Government;

c. that discrimination and violence against women and children in the Special Capital Region Province of Jakarta continues to increase and spread, causing community members to be unsafe in carrying out their lives, thus requiring integrated protection efforts;

d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation on the Protection of Women and Children from Acts of Violence;

